keywords:
  - hybrid rocket
  - paraffin
  - many-objective optimization
  - NSGA-II
  - differential evolution
  - memetic algorithm
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  A self-contained re-implementation of a thermodynamically constrained transient
  many-objective design model for a 300 N-class paraffin/LOX hybrid rocket, with
  optimization (NSGA-II, NSGA-III, SPEA2, differential-evolution and memetic
  variants including a Scheduled DE-Memetic hybrid), quality indicators (HV, IGD+),
  non-parametric statistics, RK4 verification, and a Monte-Carlo per-constraint
  uncertainty stress test. The code reproduces its own results deterministically.
